# FishWizz — Cloudflare Workers Static Assets headers.
#
# scripts/postbuild.mjs renders this to dist/_headers, substituting
# %SUPABASE_ORIGIN% and %FISHWIZZ_BUILD%. Deployed via `wrangler deploy`
# (wrangler.toml's [assets] block) -- the one authoritative pipeline; see
# that file's own header for why _headers only takes effect through that
# path and not the raw Assets Upload API this repo used to call directly.
#
# The CSP ships as Report-Only first. Flip it to Content-Security-Policy at
# Stage 6 after reviewing a deploy's worth of reports -- enforcing an untested
# policy on cutover day turns a config mistake into an outage.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(self), camera=(self)
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin-allow-popups
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self'; script-src 'self' https://challenges.cloudflare.com; frame-src https://challenges.cloudflare.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob: https://*.tile.openstreetmap.org https://*.tile.opentopomap.org https://server.arcgisonline.com https://services.arcgisonline.com; connect-src 'self' %SUPABASE_ORIGIN% https://o4511973160845312.ingest.us.sentry.io; worker-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'
  X-FishWizz-Release: %FISHWIZZ_BUILD%

# Notes on the policy above:
#
# frame-ancestors 'none' supersedes X-Frame-Options, so that header is not set.
#
# style-src needs 'unsafe-inline': several modules inject <style> elements at
# runtime (onboarding.js, launch.js, mission-v3.js, arsenal-safe.js, ask-atlas.js,
# and others), plus Leaflet sets inline style attributes. Removing it means
# refactoring all of them -- a separate project, tracked, not a blocker for
# launch.
#
# No 'unsafe-eval' anywhere: verified there is no eval() and no new Function()
# in the tree.
#
# script-src and frame-src both carry one third-party origin,
# challenges.cloudflare.com, for Turnstile (DEPLOYMENT.md step 5):
# script-src loads its widget script, frame-src lets it render the challenge
# iframe. Leaflet is still bundled from npm rather than loaded from unpkg, so
# this is deliberately the only external script origin, added for exactly one
# reason (CAPTCHA cannot run same-origin) rather than accumulated by habit.
# src/runtime/turnstile.js only loads this script at all when
# VITE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY is set, so until step 5 is done, granting the
# origin here has no observable effect.
#
# connect-src also carries this project's Sentry ingest origin (DEPLOYMENT.md
# step 8) -- per-org, so unlike Turnstile's fixed origin this one is only
# known (and only added) once a real project exists. src/runtime/sentry.js
# only calls Sentry.init() at all when VITE_SENTRY_DSN is set, so this origin
# being present in the policy is inert on its own.
#
# The remaining external origins are img-src only (map tiles), which cannot
# execute code.
#
# X-FishWizz-Release carries the same non-sensitive build identifier as the
# HTML shell's <meta name="fishwizz-build"> tag, sw.js's own CACHE name, and
# window.__FISHWIZZ_BUILD__ -- all four are asserted to match by
# scripts/verify-release-match.mjs. Not a secret: just a content hash of the
# shipped files, useful for confirming which release a given response
# actually came from.

# release-blocking stabilization (2026-08-28 follow-up): the exact cache
# semantics requested -- "no-cache, must-revalidate", not "max-age=0,
# must-revalidate". Both force a real revalidation before reuse, but
# no-cache is the unambiguous, standard way to say "never serve this from
# cache without checking with origin first" and is what every cache
# implementation (browser and CDN alike) is built to recognize first-class.

# P1 follow-up, caught live in production: Cloudflare's Workers Static
# Assets _headers engine does NOT let a more specific rule override a
# broader one -- it concatenates BOTH matching rules' Cache-Control values
# into the same response. A generic /*.js glob here used to also match
# /assets/*.js (Vite's own hashed bundle), producing a genuinely
# self-contradicting live header: "no-cache, must-revalidate, public,
# max-age=31536000, immutable" on the one file that most needs to be
# cached forever. scripts/postbuild.mjs now appends one exact, non-
# overlapping rule per real non-hashed file below this line (never a glob
# that could cross into /assets/) -- see that script's own comment for why.

/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate

/
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate

/manifest.webmanifest
  Content-Type: application/manifest+json
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate

# Hashed bundler output is content-addressed and safe to pin forever. The
# ONLY rule that ever matches anything under /assets/ -- no other pattern
# in this file is broad enough to also reach in here, by construction.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

%FISHWIZZ_NONHASHED_RULES%
